Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• director_mapping.movie_id: link each director to the movies he/she directed – basis for counting movies and for all joins with movies / ratings  
• director_mapping.name_id: director’s unique identifier – will be the “director id” asked in the result  
• names.id: joins to director_mapping.name_id  
• names.name: the human‑readable director name  
• movies.id: joins to director_mapping.movie_id and ratings.movie_id  
• movies.duration: each movie’s running time – needed for “avg inter‑movie duration” and “total movie duration”  
• movies.year (or date_published): can be used if one wants gaps between movies, but here we just need the duration values  
• ratings.movie_id: joins to movies / director_mapping  
• ratings.avg_rating: used for average, min and max rating per director  
• ratings.total_votes: summed to get the directors’ total votes  

Typical join / filter conditions that will be useful  
• director_mapping.movie_id = movies.id  
• director_mapping.movie_id = ratings.movie_id  
• director_mapping.name_id  = names.id  
• GROUP BY names.id (or director_mapping.name_id) to aggregate per director  
• ORDER BY movie_count DESC, total_movie_duration DESC  
• LIMIT 9 to keep only the top 9 directors  


-- 1) Peek at distinct director ids  
```sql
--Description: List 20 distinct director IDs that appear in the mapping table.
SELECT DISTINCT dm."name_id"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 2) See a few director names  
```sql
--Description: Fetch 20 director IDs together with their names.
SELECT n."id", n."name"
FROM "names" AS n
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 3) Check some movie ids and durations  
```sql
--Description: Inspect movie ids with their duration values.
SELECT m."id", m."duration"
FROM "movies" AS m
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 4) Test join of a director to his/her movies  
```sql
--Description: A sample join of one director to the titles he/she directed.
SELECT dm."name_id", n."name", dm."movie_id", m."title"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names"   AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
JOIN "movies"  AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 5) Bring in ratings for those movies  
```sql
--Description: Add ratings to the director–movie listing.
SELECT dm."name_id", n."name", m."title", r."avg_rating", r."total_votes"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names"   AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
JOIN "movies"  AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "ratings" AS r ON r."movie_id" = m."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 6) Count how many movies each director has  
```sql
--Description: Simple movie count per director.
SELECT dm."name_id", n."name", COUNT(*) AS "movie_count"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names" AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
ORDER BY "movie_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 7) Aggregate duration and rating metrics (without rounding yet)  
```sql
--Description: Raw aggregates: average duration, sum duration, average rating, min & max rating.
SELECT dm."name_id",
       n."name",
       COUNT(DISTINCT dm."movie_id")     AS "movie_cnt",
       AVG(m."duration")                 AS "avg_duration",
       SUM(m."duration")                 AS "total_duration",
       AVG(r."avg_rating")               AS "avg_rating",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")               AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")               AS "max_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")              AS "sum_votes"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names"   AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
JOIN "movies"  AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "ratings" AS r ON r."movie_id" = dm."movie_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 8) Same as #7 but add ROUNDs to match requested formatting  
```sql
--Description: Rounded averages: duration to nearest int, rating to 2 decimals.
SELECT dm."name_id",
       n."name",
       COUNT(DISTINCT dm."movie_id")      AS "movie_cnt",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration"))           AS "avg_duration",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)      AS "avg_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")               AS "sum_votes",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")                AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")                AS "max_rating",
       SUM(m."duration")                  AS "total_duration"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names"   AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
JOIN "movies"  AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "ratings" AS r ON r."movie_id" = dm."movie_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 9) Order by movie count then by total duration  
```sql
--Description: Sort directors by movie count desc, total duration desc (top 20 shown).
SELECT dm."name_id"                         AS "director_id",
       n."name"                             AS "director_name",
       COUNT(DISTINCT dm."movie_id")        AS "movie_cnt",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration"))             AS "avg_duration",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)        AS "avg_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")                 AS "sum_votes",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")                  AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")                  AS "max_rating",
       SUM(m."duration")                    AS "total_duration"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names"   AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
JOIN "movies"  AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "ratings" AS r ON r."movie_id" = dm."movie_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
ORDER BY "movie_cnt" DESC, "total_duration" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

-- 10) FINAL QUERY – exactly the specification (top 9 directors)  
```sql
--Description: Top 9 directors by movie count and, as tie‑breaker, total movie duration.
SELECT dm."name_id"                        AS "director_id",
       n."name"                            AS "director_name",
       COUNT(DISTINCT dm."movie_id")       AS "movie_count",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration"))            AS "avg_inter_movie_duration",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)       AS "avg_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")                AS "total_votes",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")                 AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")                 AS "max_rating",
       SUM(m."duration")                   AS "total_movie_duration"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "names"   AS n ON n."id" = dm."name_id"
JOIN "movies"  AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "ratings" AS r ON r."movie_id" = dm."movie_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id", n."name"
ORDER BY "movie_count" DESC, "total_movie_duration" DESC
LIMIT 9;
```
